inference_trace:
Use a bitmask DP over the set of elements already removed.

1. Let `m = nums.Length`. Precompute `g[i][j] = gcd(nums[i], nums[j])` for every pair.
2. Let `dp[mask]` be the best score after removing exactly the elements in `mask`. Start with `dp[0] = 0`; every other state starts as unreachable (`-1`).
3. Process masks in increasing order. Skip a mask if it is unreachable or has an odd number of bits.
4. For a valid mask, the next operation number is `op = bits(mask) / 2 + 1`.
5. To avoid trying the same set of pairs in different orders, always pair the lowest unused index `i` with some other unused index `j`. Update `dp[mask | (1<<i) | (1<<j)]` with `dp[mask] + op * g[i][j]`.
6. The answer is `dp[full]`, where `full` has all `m` bits set.

The order of operations is still fully explored, because which pair gets which multiplier depends on the order in which pairs are added. Fixing the lowest unused index only removes duplicate paths that reach the same state at the same step.

Complexity: there are 2^14 masks and about 13 choices of `j` per mask, so this is fast.

```csharp
public class Solution {
    private int Gcd(int a, int b) {
        while (b != 0) { int t = a % b; a = b; b = t; }
        return a;
    }
    public int MaxScore(int[] nums) {
        int m = nums.Length;
        int[,] g = new int[m, m];
        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++)
            for (int j = i + 1; j < m; j++)
                g[i, j] = Gcd(nums[i], nums[j]);
        int full = (1 << m) - 1;
        int[] dp = new int[1 << m];
        for (int k = 0; k <= full; k++) dp[k] = -1;
        dp[0] = 0;
        for (int mask = 0; mask < full; mask++) {
            if (dp[mask] < 0) continue;
            int bits = 0;
            for (int t = mask; t != 0; t &= t - 1) bits++;
            if ((bits & 1) == 1) continue;
            int op = bits / 2 + 1;
            int i = 0;
            while (((mask >> i) & 1) == 1) i++;
            for (int j = i + 1; j < m; j++) {
                if (((mask >> j) & 1) == 1) continue;
                int nm = mask | (1 << i) | (1 << j);
                int val = dp[mask] + op * g[i, j];
                if (val > dp[nm]) dp[nm] = val;
            }
        }
        return dp[full];
    }
}
```

