Walk through the array and remember the index of the last `1` seen. Two `1`s at indices `prev` and `i` have `i - prev - 1` zeros between them, so whenever that gap is less than `k`, return `false`. If the scan finishes without a violation, return `true`.

```csharp
public class Solution {
    public bool KLengthApart(int[] nums, int k) {
        int prev = -1;
        for (int i = 0; i < nums.Length; i++) {
            if (nums[i] == 1) {
                if (prev != -1 && i - prev - 1 < k) return false;
                prev = i;
            }
        }
        return true;
    }
}
