Count how often each letter appears, then check that every nonzero count is the same.

1. Use an array of 26 counters, one per lowercase letter, and increment the counter for each character in `s`.
2. Walk through the counters, skipping zeros (letters that never appear).
3. Remember the first nonzero count seen. If any later nonzero count differs from it, return `false`.
4. If no mismatch is found, return `true`.

This runs in O(n) time with O(1) extra space.

```csharp
public class Solution {
    public bool AreOccurrencesEqual(string s) {
        int[] cnt = new int[26];
        foreach (char c in s) cnt[c - 'a']++;
        int f = 0;
        foreach (int x in cnt) {
            if (x == 0) continue;
            if (f == 0) f = x;
            else if (x != f) return false;
        }
        return true;
    }
}
```

