Use prefix sums so every row, column and diagonal sum of a candidate square is an O(1) lookup.

**Prefix sums** (all sized `(m+1) x (n+1)`):
- `row[i][j+1] = row[i][j] + grid[i][j]` — prefix along each row.
- `col[i+1][j] = col[i][j] + grid[i][j]` — prefix along each column.
- `d1[i+1][j+1] = d1[i][j] + grid[i][j]` — main-diagonal prefix.
- `d2[i+1][j] = d2[i][j+1] + grid[i][j]` — anti-diagonal prefix (going down-left).

**Sums for a square with top-left `(r, c)` and size `k`:**
- Row `i`: `row[i][c+k] - row[i][c]`.
- Column `j`: `col[r+k][j] - col[r][j]`.
- Main diagonal: `d1[r+k][c+k] - d1[r][c]`.
- Anti-diagonal: it runs from `(r, c+k-1)` down to `(r+k-1, c)`. Its sum is `d2[r+k][c] - d2[r][c+k]`.

**Check of the anti-diagonal formula.** `d2[i+1][j]` is the sum of `grid[i][j]` plus `grid[i-1][j+1]` and so on, going up-right. So `d2[r+k][c]` sums from `grid[r+k-1][c]` up-right to the boundary. Subtracting `d2[r][c+k]` removes everything beyond `grid[r][c+k-1]`, leaving exactly the anti-diagonal.

**Search order.** Try `k` from `min(m, n)` down to 2 and return the first `k` with a valid square; otherwise return 1.

**Cost.** For each `k` there are O(mn) positions, each checked in O(k). The total is about 50·50·50·50 operations, which is fine.

**Overflow.** Values go up to 10^6 and a sum has at most 50 terms, so it stays at most 5·10^7 and fits in `int`. Using `long` anyway costs nothing.

```csharp
public class Solution {
    public int LargestMagicSquare(int[][] grid) {
        int m = grid.Length, n = grid[0].Length;
        long[,] row = new long[m + 1, n + 1];
        long[,] col = new long[m + 1, n + 1];
        long[,] d1 = new long[m + 1, n + 2];
        long[,] d2 = new long[m + 1, n + 2];
        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
                row[i, j + 1] = row[i, j] + grid[i][j];
                col[i + 1, j] = col[i, j] + grid[i][j];
                d1[i + 1, j + 1] = d1[i, j] + grid[i][j];
            }
            for (int j = n - 1; j >= 0; j--) {
                d2[i + 1, j] = d2[i, j + 1] + grid[i][j];
            }
        }
        for (int k = Math.Min(m, n); k >= 2; k--) {
            for (int r = 0; r + k <= m; r++) {
                for (int c = 0; c + k <= n; c++) {
                    long target = d1[r + k, c + k] - d1[r, c];
                    long anti = d2[r + k, c] - d2[r, c + k];
                    if (anti != target) continue;
                    bool ok = true;
                    for (int i = r; i < r + k && ok; i++) {
                        if (row[i, c + k] - row[i, c] != target) ok = false;
                    }
                    for (int j = c; j < c + k && ok; j++) {
                        if (col[r + k, j] - col[r, j] != target) ok = false;
                    }
                    if (ok) return k;
                }
            }
        }
        return 1;
    }
}
```

