Approach: drop the dashes, uppercase everything, then build the groups so that only the first group can be shorter than `k`.

1. Collect every non-dash character of `s` and convert it to uppercase.
2. Let `n` be the number of collected characters. The first group has length `n % k`, or `k` if that remainder is 0.
3. Write the characters in order. Insert a dash before every character after the first whose distance from the end is a multiple of `k`. For the character at index `i`, that means `(n - i) % k == 0` and `i > 0`.
4. If `n == 0` (the input was only dashes), the result is an empty string.

```csharp
using System.Text;

public class Solution {
    public string LicenseKeyFormatting(string s, int k) {
        var chars = new StringBuilder();
        foreach (char c in s) {
            if (c != '-') chars.Append(char.ToUpperInvariant(c));
        }
        int n = chars.Length;
        var res = new StringBuilder(n + n / k + 1);
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            if (i > 0 && (n - i) % k == 0) res.Append('-');
            res.Append(chars[i]);
        }
        return res.ToString();
    }
}
```

