inference_trace:
Use prefix sums and handle the two possible orders: L-length subarray before the M-length one, and the reverse.

For one order (L before M):
1. Scan `i` from `L + M` to `n`.
2. Keep `maxL`, the best sum of any L-length subarray ending at or before index `i - M`.
3. Combine `maxL` with the M-length subarray ending at `i`.

Run this helper once for `(firstLen, secondLen)` and once for `(secondLen, firstLen)`, then take the larger result.

```csharp
public class Solution {
    public int MaxSumTwoNoOverlap(int[] nums, int firstLen, int secondLen) {
        int n = nums.Length;
        int[] p = new int[n + 1];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) p[i + 1] = p[i] + nums[i];
        return System.Math.Max(Helper(p, n, firstLen, secondLen), Helper(p, n, secondLen, firstLen));
    }
    private int Helper(int[] p, int n, int L, int M) {
        int best = 0, maxL = 0;
        for (int i = L + M; i <= n; i++) {
            maxL = System.Math.Max(maxL, p[i - M] - p[i - M - L]);
            best = System.Math.Max(best, maxL + p[i] - p[i - M]);
        }
        return best;
    }
}
```

