inference_trace:
For each infected node `u`, count the clean nodes that only `u` can reach once all other infected nodes are treated as blocked. Removing `u` saves exactly those nodes.

**Method**

1. Mark every node in `initial` as infected.
2. For each infected node `u`, run a BFS from `u` that moves only through clean nodes.
3. Each clean node records which infected sources can reach it this way. The record is a single source id, or `-2` if two or more sources reach it.
4. Afterwards, every clean node reached by exactly one source `u` adds 1 to `count[u]`.
5. Return the infected node with the largest count. On ties, pick the smallest index, so iterate over `initial` in sorted order.

**Why this is correct**

A clean node reachable only from `u` through clean nodes is never infected once `u` is removed. It cannot be reached from any other infected node without passing through `u`. Any node reachable from two or more sources stays infected no matter which single source is removed.

**Complexity**

Each BFS scans the adjacency matrix, so the total is O(k·n²) for k initial nodes. With n = 300 this is at most about 27 million operations, which is fine.

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;

public class Solution {
    public int MinMalwareSpread(int[][] graph, int[] initial) {
        int n = graph.Length;
        bool[] inf = new bool[n];
        foreach (var x in initial) inf[x] = true;
        int[] owner = new int[n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) owner[i] = -1;
        foreach (var u in initial) {
            bool[] vis = new bool[n];
            var q = new Queue<int>();
            vis[u] = true;
            q.Enqueue(u);
            while (q.Count > 0) {
                int a = q.Dequeue();
                for (int b = 0; b < n; b++) {
                    if (graph[a][b] == 1 && !vis[b] && !inf[b]) {
                        vis[b] = true;
                        q.Enqueue(b);
                        if (owner[b] == -1) owner[b] = u;
                        else if (owner[b] != u) owner[b] = -2;
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        int[] cnt = new int[n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) if (owner[i] >= 0) cnt[owner[i]]++;
        int[] init = (int[])initial.Clone();
        Array.Sort(init);
        int best = init[0];
        foreach (var u in init) if (cnt[u] > cnt[best]) best = u;
        return best;
    }
}
```

