Compare the string against the alternating pattern that starts with `'0'` (`"0101..."`):

- Let `cnt` be the number of positions `i` where `s[i]` differs from that pattern, i.e. where `s[i] - '0' != i % 2`.
- The only other alternating string is `"1010..."`, which differs from `s` at exactly the other positions, so it needs `n - cnt` changes.
- The answer is `min(cnt, n - cnt)`.

```csharp
public class Solution {
    public int MinOperations(string s) {
        int cnt = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < s.Length; i++) {
            if (s[i] - '0' != i % 2) cnt++;
        }
        return System.Math.Min(cnt, s.Length - cnt);
    }
}
