Track the running prefix sum and its minimum value, starting the minimum at 0.

For every prefix we need `startValue + prefix >= 1`, so `startValue >= 1 - prefix`. The tightest constraint comes from the smallest prefix, giving `startValue = 1 - minPrefix`.

Starting `minPrefix` at 0 covers the case where every prefix is non-negative. Then the answer is 1, which satisfies the requirement that `startValue` be positive.

```csharp
public class Solution {
    public int MinStartValue(int[] nums) {
        int sum = 0, minPrefix = 0;
        foreach (int n in nums) {
            sum += n;
            if (sum < minPrefix) minPrefix = sum;
        }
        return 1 - minPrefix;
    }
}
```

