inference_trace:
Convert each date into a count of days since a fixed reference point, then return the absolute difference of the two counts.

To count days for a date `Y-M-D`:
1. For every year from 1971 up to `Y - 1`, add 366 if it is a leap year, otherwise 365.
2. Add the days in each full month before `M` in year `Y`. February gets 29 days when `Y` is a leap year.
3. Add `D`.

A year is a leap year if it is divisible by 4 and not by 100, or if it is divisible by 400. With the 1971–2100 range, 2000 is a leap year and 2100 is not.

```csharp
public class Solution {
    public int DaysBetweenDates(string date1, string date2) {
        return System.Math.Abs(Count(date1) - Count(date2));
    }

    private static bool IsLeap(int y) {
        return (y % 4 == 0 && y % 100 != 0) || y % 400 == 0;
    }

    private static int Count(string date) {
        int y = int.Parse(date.Substring(0, 4));
        int m = int.Parse(date.Substring(5, 2));
        int d = int.Parse(date.Substring(8, 2));
        int[] md = { 31, 28, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31 };
        int total = 0;
        for (int i = 1971; i < y; i++) total += IsLeap(i) ? 366 : 365;
        for (int i = 1; i < m; i++) {
            total += md[i - 1];
            if (i == 2 && IsLeap(y)) total++;
        }
        total += d;
        return total;
    }
}
```

