inference_trace:
For each distinct value, precompute the list of indices where it appears. Building this dictionary is O(n) once in the constructor. Each `Pick` call then looks up the list for `target` and returns a uniformly random element from it in O(1), so every matching index has equal probability.

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;

public class Solution {
    private Dictionary<int, List<int>> map;
    private Random rand;

    public Solution(int[] nums) {
        map = new Dictionary<int, List<int>>();
        rand = new Random();
        for (int i = 0; i < nums.Length; i++) {
            if (!map.TryGetValue(nums[i], out var list)) {
                list = new List<int>();
                map[nums[i]] = list;
            }
            list.Add(i);
        }
    }

    public int Pick(int target) {
        var list = map[target];
        return list[rand.Next(list.Count)];
    }
}
```

