The two rectangles overlap with positive area exactly when their projections overlap with positive length on both axes:

- On the x-axis this holds when `max(x1, x1') < min(x2, x2')`.
- On the y-axis this holds when `max(y1, y1') < min(y2, y2')`.

Using strict `<` means rectangles that only touch at an edge or corner are not counted as overlapping.

Comparing coordinates directly avoids any subtraction, so there is no risk of integer overflow even at the extremes of the constraints.

```csharp
public class Solution {
    public bool IsRectangleOverlap(int[] rec1, int[] rec2) {
        return Math.Max(rec1[0], rec2[0]) < Math.Min(rec1[2], rec2[2])
            && Math.Max(rec1[1], rec2[1]) < Math.Min(rec1[3], rec2[3]);
    }
}
```

