inference_trace:
Approach: first count the minimum number of parentheses that must be removed, then use DFS to try every way of removing exactly that many, collecting valid results in a set.

1. **Count required removals.** Scan left to right with a counter `open`:
   - On `'('`, increment `open`.
   - On `')'`, decrement `open` if it is positive; otherwise this `')'` is unmatched, so increment `rmR`.
   - Whatever remains in `open` at the end becomes `rmL` (unmatched `'('`).
2. **DFS over positions.** At each index `i`, track:
   - `rl` / `rr`: how many `'('` / `')'` we may still remove.
   - `open`: the current balance of kept parentheses.
   - `sb`: the string built so far.
3. **Choices per character.**
   - For a parenthesis, we may remove it if its removal budget is still positive.
   - Otherwise, we keep it if the balance stays valid (a `')'` is only kept when `open > 0`).
   - Letters are always kept.
4. **Avoid duplicate work.** When skipping a parenthesis, skip it only if the previous character is different, or is the first in a run. This prunes duplicate branches. A `HashSet` still guarantees uniqueness of the results.
5. **Collect results.** At the end, record `sb` only if `rl == 0`, `rr == 0` and `open == 0`.

```csharp
public class Solution {
    private HashSet<string> res = new HashSet<string>();
    private string str;

    public IList<string> RemoveInvalidParentheses(string s) {
        str = s;
        int open = 0, rmR = 0;
        foreach (char c in s) {
            if (c == '(') open++;
            else if (c == ')') {
                if (open > 0) open--;
                else rmR++;
            }
        }
        int rmL = open;
        Dfs(0, rmL, rmR, 0, new System.Text.StringBuilder());
        return new List<string>(res);
    }

    private void Dfs(int i, int rl, int rr, int open, System.Text.StringBuilder sb) {
        if (i == str.Length) {
            if (rl == 0 && rr == 0 && open == 0) res.Add(sb.ToString());
            return;
        }
        char c = str[i];
        int len = sb.Length;
        if (c == '(') {
            if (rl > 0) Dfs(i + 1, rl - 1, rr, open, sb);
            sb.Append(c);
            Dfs(i + 1, rl, rr, open + 1, sb);
            sb.Length = len;
        } else if (c == ')') {
            if (rr > 0) Dfs(i + 1, rl, rr - 1, open, sb);
            if (open > 0) {
                sb.Append(c);
                Dfs(i + 1, rl, rr, open - 1, sb);
                sb.Length = len;
            }
        } else {
            sb.Append(c);
            Dfs(i + 1, rl, rr, open, sb);
            sb.Length = len;
        }
    }
}
```

