If the string is empty, no steps are needed, so return 0.

If the string is a palindrome, it can be removed in one step, so return 1.

Otherwise the answer is 2. All the `'a'` characters together form a palindromic subsequence, and so do all the `'b'` characters. Removing one group and then the other empties the string in two steps.

```csharp
public class Solution {
    public int RemovePalindromeSub(string s) {
        if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(s)) return 0;
        int i = 0, j = s.Length - 1;
        while (i < j) {
            if (s[i] != s[j]) return 2;
            i++; j--;
        }
        return 1;
    }
}
```

