inference_trace:
Track the robot's position with two counters, `x` and `y`. For each move:
- `'U'` increments `y`, `'D'` decrements `y`.
- `'R'` increments `x`, `'L'` decrements `x`.
- Any other character (such as stray spaces) is ignored.

After all moves, the robot is back at the origin exactly when both `x` and `y` are zero. This runs in O(n) time and O(1) space.

```csharp
public class Solution {
    public bool JudgeCircle(string moves) {
        int x = 0, y = 0;
        foreach (char c in moves) {
            switch (c) {
                case 'U': y++; break;
                case 'D': y--; break;
                case 'L': x--; break;
                case 'R': x++; break;
            }
        }
        return x == 0 && y == 0;
    }
}
```

