inference_trace:
Use a 3D DP where `dp[len][i][j]` is true when `s1.Substring(i, len)` can be scrambled into `s2.Substring(j, len)`.

**Base case:** for `len = 1`, `dp[1][i][j]` is true exactly when `s1[i] == s2[j]`.

**Transition:** for each split length `k` from 1 to `len - 1`, two cases make `dp[len][i][j]` true:
- **No swap:** `dp[k][i][j]` and `dp[len-k][i+k][j+k]` are both true.
- **Swap:** `dp[k][i][j+len-k]` and `dp[len-k][i+k][j]` are both true. The first `k` characters of the `s1` piece match the last `k` characters of the `s2` piece, and the remaining `len-k` characters match the front.

**Complexity:** O(n^4) time with n ≤ 30, which is about 810k operations. Memory is O(n^3).

```csharp
public class Solution {
    public bool IsScramble(string s1, string s2) {
        int n = s1.Length;
        if (n != s2.Length) return false;
        bool[,,] dp = new bool[n + 1, n, n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)
            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++)
                dp[1, i, j] = s1[i] == s2[j];
        for (int len = 2; len <= n; len++) {
            for (int i = 0; i + len <= n; i++) {
                for (int j = 0; j + len <= n; j++) {
                    bool ok = false;
                    for (int k = 1; k < len && !ok; k++) {
                        if (dp[k, i, j] && dp[len - k, i + k, j + k]) ok = true;
                        else if (dp[k, i, j + len - k] && dp[len - k, i + k, j]) ok = true;
                    }
                    dp[len, i, j] = ok;
                }
            }
        }
        return dp[n, 0, 0];
    }
}
```

