inference_trace:
The idea is to fill in the addition one column at a time, starting from the rightmost digit, and backtrack whenever a column cannot work.

1. **Quick rejection.** If any word is longer than `result`, its sum is too large. In that case return `false`.

2. **Column-wise search.** Use `Dfs(col, row, sum)`, where `col` is the current column counted from the right and `row` is the current word. `sum` is the running total for this column, including the carry from the previous column.
   - For each word that has a letter in this column:
     - If the letter already has a digit, add that digit to `sum`.
     - Otherwise, try every unused digit and add it.
   - After all words in the column, look at the letter of `result` in this column. It must decode to `sum % 10`.
     - If that letter is already mapped, check that it matches.
     - If not, assign it, as long as the digit is free.
   - Then move to the next column with carry `sum / 10`.

3. **Leading zeros.** A letter that is the first character of a multi-letter word or of `result` may never be 0.

4. **Termination.** After the last column of `result`, the leftover carry must be 0.

Each column fixes one digit of `result`, so wrong partial assignments are cut off early.

```csharp
public class Solution {
    private string[] w;
    private string res;
    private int[] map = new int[26];
    private bool[] used = new bool[10];
    private bool[] leading = new bool[26];

    public bool IsSolvable(string[] words, string result) {
        w = new string[words.Length];
        for (int i = 0; i < words.Length; i++) w[i] = words[i].Trim();
        res = result.Trim();
        foreach (var s in w) {
            if (s.Length > res.Length) return false;
            if (s.Length > 1) leading[s[0] - 'A'] = true;
        }
        if (res.Length > 1) leading[res[0] - 'A'] = true;
        for (int i = 0; i < 26; i++) map[i] = -1;
        return Dfs(0, 0, 0);
    }

    private bool Dfs(int col, int row, int sum) {
        if (col == res.Length) return sum == 0;
        if (row == w.Length) {
            int c = res[res.Length - 1 - col] - 'A';
            int d = sum % 10;
            if (map[c] != -1) {
                if (map[c] != d) return false;
                return Dfs(col + 1, 0, sum / 10);
            }
            if (used[d] || (d == 0 && leading[c])) return false;
            map[c] = d; used[d] = true;
            bool ok = Dfs(col + 1, 0, sum / 10);
            map[c] = -1; used[d] = false;
            return ok;
        }
        string s = w[row];
        if (col >= s.Length) return Dfs(col, row + 1, sum);
        int ch = s[s.Length - 1 - col] - 'A';
        if (map[ch] != -1) return Dfs(col, row + 1, sum + map[ch]);
        for (int d = 0; d < 10; d++) {
            if (used[d]) continue;
            if (d == 0 && leading[ch]) continue;
            map[ch] = d; used[d] = true;
            if (Dfs(col, row + 1, sum + d)) { map[ch] = -1; used[d] = false; return true; }
            map[ch] = -1; used[d] = false;
        }
        return false;
    }
}
```

