inference_trace:
Approach: breadth-first search over words, so the first time we reach `endWord` we have the shortest sequence.

1. Put all of `wordList` into a hash set. If `endWord` is not in it, return 0.
2. Start the BFS queue with `beginWord` at level 1.
3. For each word taken from the queue, try every position and every letter `a`–`z`:
   - Skip the letter if it equals the original character.
   - If the new word equals `endWord`, return the current level + 1.
   - If the new word is still in the set, remove it from the set (this marks it visited) and enqueue it.
4. After finishing each level, increase the level by 1.
5. If the queue empties without reaching `endWord`, return 0.

Cost: each word generates at most 26 × L neighbours, and building each costs O(L). With up to 5000 words and L ≤ 10, the total work is about 5000 × 26 × 10 × 10 ≈ 13M operations, which is fast enough.

```csharp
using System.Collections.Generic;

public class Solution {
    public int LadderLength(string beginWord, string endWord, IList<string> wordList) {
        var set = new HashSet<string>(wordList);
        if (!set.Contains(endWord)) return 0;
        set.Remove(beginWord);
        var q = new Queue<string>();
        q.Enqueue(beginWord);
        int level = 1;
        while (q.Count > 0) {
            int sz = q.Count;
            for (int s = 0; s < sz; s++) {
                var w = q.Dequeue();
                char[] arr = w.ToCharArray();
                for (int i = 0; i < arr.Length; i++) {
                    char orig = arr[i];
                    for (char c = 'a'; c <= 'z'; c++) {
                        if (c == orig) continue;
                        arr[i] = c;
                        string nw = new string(arr);
                        if (set.Contains(nw)) {
                            if (nw == endWord) return level + 1;
                            set.Remove(nw);
                            q.Enqueue(nw);
                        }
                    }
                    arr[i] = orig;
                }
            }
            level++;
        }
        return 0;
    }
}
```

